  ('b2713642-3c0e-460f-a02c-fef6580169a3', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A new trade route is proposed, but it passes through a region with a history of conflict.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('d5b840ae-ad20-42e5-b5b8-98a23f42eed7', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Mahinda is tasked with preparing a speech for a public gathering, explaining the empire's commitment to peace.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('7800c104-c014-432d-9cc5-a19b7294f084', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A group of citizens expresses fear about a potential famine, leading to panic and hoarding.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('3b2752a8-50f1-4bcd-bdc8-9393e49414f6', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Vitashoka reflects on the contrast between the "battlefield" and "today's peace."$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('d9784f7f-0e96-4358-806b-34bbd6ddc44c', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Ashoka's advisors propose a new law that, while efficient, might be seen as indifferent to the plight of a minority group.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('06c983a2-7971-4c1d-8a9e-7af4d702bcf5', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A foreign diplomat questions the practicality of relying on "intelligence and oneness of people" instead of military might for defense.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('9b39f4c7-aea2-42c8-b7f5-ebabdfb6e8f3', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The people of the empire are celebrating a decade of peace. They look to the pillars as symbols of this achievement.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 1, NULL),
  ('774fd6dd-5e05-47b6-af96-9179c50b41aa', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Emperor Ashoka, once known for his conquests, declared a profound shift in his priorities, stating, "Today, I boast not of the lands conquered but of the harmony created and the sufferings eased." This declaration marked a new era for his empire, guided by principles of peace and Dhamma.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('6ede95b2-aa63-4908-b00c-ec4f83ba54b8', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Ashoka urged his subjects to "cherish, nurture and defend this peace against greed and power." He recognized that peace was not merely the absence of war, but an active state requiring constant vigilance against internal and external threats driven by self-interest.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('674bfc08-0a2a-4a5e-a920-cb3abf1f5520', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Ashoka envisioned "a long age of enlightenment guided by the principles of Dhamma." This suggests a society where intellectual and moral progress is intertwined with ethical governance and spiritual understanding.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('99efa18e-b11e-4741-a994-5b6f9024137a', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The narrator observes that Ashoka's reign ends, but his vision—a world where peace prevails over war, kindness overcomes cruelty and wisdom triumph over ignorance—lives. This enduring vision inspires people to be better.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('54d19751-c2ea-407c-9287-01dbc4ba13ba', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The profound statement "Peace cannot be kept by force. It can only be achieved by understanding" underpins Ashoka's philosophy. This suggests a reliance on empathy, dialogue, and mutual respect as foundations for lasting peace.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('85a089a4-7516-4272-8778-8fae9f46c97a', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The wisdom "You see in the world what you carry in your heart" suggests that one's internal state profoundly shapes their perception of external reality and their interactions with it.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('5e4259b5-393a-4eb5-a9df-c38d52b202b2', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The text mentions "COMPETENCY-BASED LEARNING" and suggests exploring "the theme of compassion" using smart class software. This implies an educational approach focused on practical skills and ethical development.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('b7bff1d6-8746-44f9-acde-43a1150c694c', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The question posed in the text, "How might Ashoka’s rule through peace and compassion instead of war affect his empire’s future stability and prosperity?" highlights the long-term consequences of his governance philosophy.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('ef64100a-86f6-4498-aa4e-724b3f8ff42e', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$[ACT 3, Scene 3: Royal Court, Post-Transformation] [Ashoka, the symbol of peace, stands before his people and advisors. His voice carries the wisdom he has gained through the trials of war.] Ashoka: See what peace has done. Our war- torn land now prospers with compassion. We have traded our swords for tools of builders, scholars and healers. Roads connect our provinces. Ashoka: The Quest - For Peace-ll Pre-Reading Imagine you are a ruler who has just won a great battle. Would you use your power to continue winning new lands or promote peace and prosperity in your kingdom? Discuss in class. @ Learning Outcomes Siaaiaaeea ; | After the lesson, I will be able to: te read the text with correct pronunciation, intonation and expressions * learn new words and use them in sentences * explore and appreciate the theme '® answer questions based on the story ‘+ use active and passive voice correctly in! | sentences ' i* write a speech : through compassion and peace. Let us read the story and find out how Emperor Ashoka managed it. Hospitals nurture health and schools teach wisdom and peace to our children. This is the strength of an empire—the highest power of moral strength and the unimaginable wealth of kindness. Mahinda: Dear father, your ideals have brought prosperity but dissent, too. Some say an empire must stay strong against threats. Tell us, my king, doesn’t the wolf get closest to the flock when the shepherd lays down his staff? Why was Mahinda unsure of Ashoka’s decision? Discuss with your partner. Ashoka: Dearest Mahinda, your concerns are important. | believe there is greater strength in turning our enemies into friends. We must fortify our borders and win the hearts of those beyond them. We will invest in peace and people. With these, we will gain more profound security and stability than any fortress could provide. English-8 1D)$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('2e67d586-564b-4dea-a24c-41f4be2a8cbc', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$[ACT 3, Scene 3: Royal Court, Post-Transformation] [Ashoka, the symbol of peace, stands before his people and advisors. His voice carries the wisdom he has gained through the trials of war.] Ashoka: See what peace has done. Our war- torn land now prospers with compassion. We have traded our swords for tools of builders, scholars and healers. Roads connect our provinces. Ashoka: The Quest - For Peace-ll Pre-Reading Imagine you are a ruler who has just won a great battle. Would you use your power to continue winning new lands or promote peace and prosperity in your kingdom? Discuss in class. @ Learning Outcomes Siaaiaaeea ; | After the lesson, I will be able to: te read the text with correct pronunciation, intonation and expressions * learn new words and use them in sentences * explore and appreciate the theme '® answer questions based on the story ‘+ use active and passive voice correctly in! | sentences ' i* write a speech : through compassion and peace. Let us read the story and find out how Emperor Ashoka managed it. Hospitals nurture health and schools teach wisdom and peace to our children. This is the strength of an empire—the highest power of moral strength and the unimaginable wealth of kindness. Mahinda: Dear father, your ideals have brought prosperity but dissent, too. Some say an empire must stay strong against threats. Tell us, my king, doesn’t the wolf get closest to the flock when the shepherd lays down his staff? Why was Mahinda unsure of Ashoka’s decision? Discuss with your partner. Ashoka: Dearest Mahinda, your concerns are important. | believe there is greater strength in turning our enemies into friends. We must fortify our borders and win the hearts of those beyond them. We will invest in peace and people. With these, we will gain more profound security and stability than any fortress could provide. English-8 1D)$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('b87623e4-af6a-476d-8423-58442e39f472', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$[ACT 3, Scene 3: Royal Court, Post-Transformation] [Ashoka, the symbol of peace, stands before his people and advisors. His voice carries the wisdom he has gained through the trials of war.] Ashoka: See what peace has done. Our war- torn land now prospers with compassion. We have traded our swords for tools of builders, scholars and healers. Roads connect our provinces. Ashoka: The Quest - For Peace-ll Pre-Reading Imagine you are a ruler who has just won a great battle. Would you use your power to continue winning new lands or promote peace and prosperity in your kingdom? Discuss in class. @ Learning Outcomes Siaaiaaeea ; | After the lesson, I will be able to: te read the text with correct pronunciation, intonation and expressions * learn new words and use them in sentences * explore and appreciate the theme '® answer questions based on the story ‘+ use active and passive voice correctly in! | sentences ' i* write a speech : through compassion and peace. Let us read the story and find out how Emperor Ashoka managed it. Hospitals nurture health and schools teach wisdom and peace to our children. This is the strength of an empire—the highest power of moral strength and the unimaginable wealth of kindness. Mahinda: Dear father, your ideals have brought prosperity but dissent, too. Some say an empire must stay strong against threats. Tell us, my king, doesn’t the wolf get closest to the flock when the shepherd lays down his staff? Why was Mahinda unsure of Ashoka’s decision? Discuss with your partner. Ashoka: Dearest Mahinda, your concerns are important. | believe there is greater strength in turning our enemies into friends. We must fortify our borders and win the hearts of those beyond them. We will invest in peace and people. With these, we will gain more profound security and stability than any fortress could provide. English-8 1D)$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('a93667be-359b-440e-b0d0-6d678d6c96b2', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$ACT 4, Scene 4: A New Dawn In The Empire - Public Square] [In the busy public square, full of daily commerce and vivid life, Ashoka and Vitashoka walk among the people.] Vitashoka: My elder brother, these pillars around us, engraved with messages of kindness, compassion and sanctity of life, are great monuments of your reign! They speak with the wisdom of a sage. The people look up to them for guidance and inspiration. Ashoka: Vitashoka, my brother, we have come far from the battlefield to today’s peace. These pillars are more than stone; they represent our highest aims. Let these stones testify if my past as a conqueror can be redeemed by my present as a peacemaker. Let them stand not as my legacy but as the foundation for a future of possibilities. Mahinda: Father, | still worry about the strength of this peace. What if new threats English-8 arise? Will the lessons of these pillars stand firm against the storms of war? Ashoka: Mahinda, your question is important. Remember that peace is the absence of war and the active creation of understanding, tolerance and respect. If threats arise, we will not turn to arms but to intelligence and oneness of people. [Together, they resume their walk.] What was the significance of the monuments and pillars created by Ashoka? Discuss with your partner. [ACT 5, Scene 5: Ashoka’s Legacy- The Royal Palace Gardens] [Ashoka addresses his people, courtiers and family. His voice resonates with years of experience and introspection.] Ashoka: As my reign ends, | reflect upon our journey from war to peace. Kalinga’s bloodshed taught us that true conquest is over animosity and fear, through compassion and understanding over cruelty and indifference.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
