  ('63072355-999b-4dee-a554-089fe9b88374', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$ACT 4, Scene 4: A New Dawn In The Empire - Public Square] [In the busy public square, full of daily commerce and vivid life, Ashoka and Vitashoka walk among the people.] Vitashoka: My elder brother, these pillars around us, engraved with messages of kindness, compassion and sanctity of life, are great monuments of your reign! They speak with the wisdom of a sage. The people look up to them for guidance and inspiration. Ashoka: Vitashoka, my brother, we have come far from the battlefield to today’s peace. These pillars are more than stone; they represent our highest aims. Let these stones testify if my past as a conqueror can be redeemed by my present as a peacemaker. Let them stand not as my legacy but as the foundation for a future of possibilities. Mahinda: Father, | still worry about the strength of this peace. What if new threats English-8 arise? Will the lessons of these pillars stand firm against the storms of war? Ashoka: Mahinda, your question is important. Remember that peace is the absence of war and the active creation of understanding, tolerance and respect. If threats arise, we will not turn to arms but to intelligence and oneness of people. [Together, they resume their walk.] What was the significance of the monuments and pillars created by Ashoka? Discuss with your partner. [ACT 5, Scene 5: Ashoka’s Legacy- The Royal Palace Gardens] [Ashoka addresses his people, courtiers and family. His voice resonates with years of experience and introspection.] Ashoka: As my reign ends, | reflect upon our journey from war to peace. Kalinga’s bloodshed taught us that true conquest is over animosity and fear, through compassion and understanding over cruelty and indifference.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('45c5a1c4-1e29-4779-b99e-5e43a5c58382', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '5fb23b1c-ff61-4e11-b879-2cb82e69505b', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Today, I boast not of the lands conquered but of the harmony created and the sufferings eased. My dear subjects, cherish, nurture and defend this peace against greed and power. Let Ashoka’s peace begin a long age of enlightenment guided by the principles of Dhamma. Narrator: As the sun sets, the words of Emperor Ashoka stayed with everyone. These words inspire them to be better. His reign ends, but his vision - a world where peace prevails over war, kindness overcomes cruelty and wisdom triumph over ignorance-lives. COMPETENCY-BASED LEARNING [As the crowd disperses, there is a sense of solemnity and hope. The curtains slowly close] Peace cannot be kept by force. It can only be achieved by understanding. Cea Use Cordova Smart Class Software on the smart board in class to explore the theme of compassion. TIME FOR DISCUSSION You see in the world what you carry in your heart. SE EXERCIS [Use Cordova Smart Class Software on the smart board in class to do these exercises. ] (According to NEP Guidelines) [fy ANSWER ORALLY (Logical Thinking) Read these words aloud: dissent, triumphs, introspection, enlightenment, sanctity How might Ashoka’s rule through peace and compassion instead of war affect his empire’s future stability and prosperity? [fy MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS A. Tick () the correct options. (Understanding, Analysing) 1. What does Ashoka believe is the true strength of an empire? (a) conquering new lands (c) moral strength and kindness C) (b) building the strongest army C) (d) accumulating wealth LC) os) English-8$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-784Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
